From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt BE18000 port <openwrt@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:28:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: esmt: match F50D2G41KA within 4-byte READID

The Qualcomm QPIC SPI-NAND controller (spi-qpic-snand) reads JEDEC IDs
from the 32-bit NAND_READ_ID register, returning at most 4 bytes
(manufacturer ID + 3 device ID bytes).

ESMT F50D2G41KA currently requires 4 device ID bytes (5 bytes total:
0xc8 0x51 0x7f 0x7f 0x7f), so byte 4 is always 0x00 on QPIC and the
match fails, falling through to GigaDevice GD5F1GQ5UExxG (128 MiB
instead of 256 MiB) and breaking UBI attachment on the 190 MiB rootfs
partition.

Match F50D2G41KA on 3 device ID bytes (0x51, 0x7f, 0x7f), consistent
with F50D1G41LB directly above it.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt BE18000 port <openwrt@localhost>
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
@@ -211,8 +211,7 @@ static const struct spinand_info esmt_c8
 		     SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO(28, 2, &f50l1g41lb_user_otp_ops),
 		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F50D2G41KA",
-		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x51, 0x7f,
-				0x7f, 0x7f),
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x51, 0x7f, 0x7f),
 		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 128, 64, 2048, 40, 1, 1, 1),
 		     NAND_ECCREQ(8, 512),
 		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
